!highlight{target=sec:why text="wind-pollinated and self-incompatible"}

:::{highlight target=sec:why text="four or five years" color=green author="DM"}
Worth saying which cultivars this holds for -- Cosford bears noticeably
earlier than Kentish Cob in my experience.
:::

:::{sticky-note target=sec:spacing text="three metres is the usual compromise" at=end author="DM"}
Is this the spacing the table models, or the one you actually planted?
The two are worth distinguishing for a reader copying the figure.
:::

!highlight{target=sec:spacing text="Netting does not work" color=pink}

:::{sticky-note target=sec:conclusion text="costs a year" at=start color=blue author="AL"}
This is the sentence I would lead the whole piece with.
:::
